\ A quotation head names what the body receives from the stack. The opening bar
\ is optional, so [: x | … :] and [: | x | … :] are the same head. A ^ name is
\ the enclosing global rather than a capture; a ? name is a fresh logic variable.
[ 2 3 4 ] [: x | x x f* :] map . cr
[ 2 3 4 ] [: | x | x x f* :] map . cr
3.0 [: a | a a f* :] execute . cr

variable scale
2.0 to scale
[ 2 3 4 ] [: x | x scale f* :] map . cr
5.0 [: n ^scale | n to scale :] execute  scale . cr

[: ?q n | q n ~ drop  q ? :] 7 swap execute . cr
